# sriq: predecessor relevance (SPEC §5.5 S6 R8, slice 9i), reactivation.
# Under trivial, X's and Y's successors share v_⊤: X's edge supplies A(x)
# and r(y, x), Y's supplies B(x) and s(y, x). Hyper there joins A → A and
# B → B into A(x) ∧ B(x) → C(x), which no single edge supplies, so it is
# stored but deferred. X ⊑ X1 ⊑ X2 ⊑ X3 ⊑ ∀r.B later adds B(f(x)) to X's
# K₂, so trig(v_X, f) grows to hold B. The stored clause is now supported,
# and must be activated: only then does Hyper join it with ∃r.C ⊑ Q and
# Pred bring Q back to X. A run that never reactivated it would miss
# X ⊑ Q.
# Expect: X ⊑ Q.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class . :B a owl:Class . :C a owl:Class . :Q a owl:Class .
:X a owl:Class . :X1 a owl:Class . :X2 a owl:Class . :X3 a owl:Class . :Y a owl:Class .
:r a owl:ObjectProperty . :s a owl:ObjectProperty .
:X rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :A ] .
:X rdfs:subClassOf :X1 . :X1 rdfs:subClassOf :X2 . :X2 rdfs:subClassOf :X3 .
:X3 rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:allValuesFrom :B ] .
:Y rdfs:subClassOf [ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :s ; owl:someValuesFrom :B ] .
[ owl:intersectionOf ( :A :B ) ] rdfs:subClassOf :C .
[ a owl:Restriction ; owl:onProperty :r ; owl:someValuesFrom :C ] rdfs:subClassOf :Q .
